y insurance products. The company was founded in 1851 and is headquartered in Glens Falls, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David S. DeMarco | CEO, President & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 725 people. Each employee generates $50K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $942 per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Arrow Financial Corporation is a small-cap financial services business with a $713M market cap.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The business throws off $36M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.94\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 22% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.21865363439106628},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time